<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philippeville massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1955</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Philippeville massacre took place on 20 August 1955 in and around Philippeville, now Skikda, in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. FLN fighters and armed villagers attacked Europeans and pro-French Muslims, killing over a hundred, including women and children at the mining village of El Halia. French reprisals killed thousands of Muslim Algerians, deepening the divide between the communities and escalating the war.</p></div>
